data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1** to **v2** (`Microsoft.OpenApi 2.x`). This is a significant breaking change. Here's what changed and the fixes:

## Key Changes

| .NET 9 (OpenAPI.NET v1) | .NET 10 (OpenAPI.NET v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.*` types (`OpenApiString`, etc.) | Removed — use `JsonNode` |
| `param.Schema` (returns `OpenApiSchema`) | `param.Schema` is now `JsonSchema` (from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models`) |
| `schema.Nullable` | Removed — use `schema.Type` flags |
| `schema.Properties` returns `IDictionary<string, OpenApiSchema>` | Returns `IDictionary<string, JsonSchema>` |
| `OpenApiResponse` constructed inline | Same, but `Responses` is now `IDictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` (no `TryAdd` change) |
| `OpenApiReference { Type = ... }` | `Type` → `OpenApiReference` no longer uses `ReferenceType` enum the same way |
| `new OpenApiSecurityRequirement` (derives from `Dictionary`) | Now a class with a `Schemes` dictionary |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString is gone — use JsonNode instead
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };

    // OpenApiSecurityRequirement no longer inherits Dictionary;
    // use the Schemes property instead
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable property is removed; instead manipulate the Type flags.
                // To mark as NOT nullable, ensure the Nullable flag is absent:
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of Fixes

1. **`OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` → `JsonNode`** — Replace `new OpenApiString("1.0")` with `JsonValue.Create("1.0")`. Remove the `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace.

2. **`schema.Nullable` removed** — The nullable concept is now a flag on `schema.Type`. Use bitwise operations: add `JsonSchemaType.Null` to make nullable, remove it (`& ~JsonSchemaType.Null`) to make non-nullable.

3. **`OpenApiSecurityRequirement` dictionary syntax** — It no longer inherits from `Dictionary`. Use the `Schemes` property explicitly.

4. **Add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes;`** — Required for `JsonValue`/`JsonNode`.
